    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the conventions this class already established:\n\n- `countOwnersRegisteredToday()` mirrors the existing sibling helpers (`countOwnersInCity`, `countNamesakes`, `isTelephoneInUse`) exactly \u2014 same `findAllOwners().stream().filter(...).count()` idiom, same private-instance-method shape, same Javadoc style. A maintainer would find it immediately familiar rather than surprising.\n- It's placed right next to `countOwnersInCity`, and `DAILY_CREATE_LIMIT` sits directly beside the analogous `CITY_CAPACITY` constant with matching documentation. The grouping is consistent.\n- The guard in `addOwner` follows the same `if (...) throw new ResponseStatusException(...)` validation-guard pattern already used for the telephone, household, and city-capacity checks \u2014 additive, not a rewrite.\n- No duplication is introduced, and no unit is turned into a catch-all beyond the business-logic-in-controller design this file already embodies (the daily-limit rule is not more misplaced than the city-capacity or namesake rules that already live here).\n\nThe structure is coherent, additive, and idiomatic to this codebase; no structural changes are warranted.",
